course: dictionary
lesson: 6476
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word nature is a good example. Nature can mean everything in the world not made by people, like plants, animals, rocks and rivers.
explain: Nature can also mean what someone is really like inside. «It's in his nature» means it is how he always is. If a story says «It's in her nature to help everyone», then nature means her character, not the trees or the sky.
explain: To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it. «Nature is lovely to look at but not always to touch» is about plants, animals and fields, so here nature means the living world around us. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Nature means everything in the world not made by people: plants, animals, rocks, rivers, the sky and the weather.
fact: A person's or animal's nature is what they are usually like inside, their character.
fact: The nature of something is what kind of thing it is.
fact: «Rewilding» means bringing missing animals back and letting nature run itself again.
fact: Phrases with nature include nature walk, nature trail and nature reserve.
exercise: «A vulture lands last, bald and scruffy, but it is one of nature's cleaners.» In this sentence, what does nature mean? | A kind of weather | A person's character | *The living world of plants and animals | A school lesson
exercise: «It's in his nature to be kind.» What does nature mean here? | A walk in the woods | *His character, what he is usually like inside | The sky at night | The shape of his body
exercise: Which of these is part of nature? | *A rock on a hill | A television | A bicycle | A river
test: «The nature of the rock is hard and grey.» What does nature mean here? | A walk along a trail | How it usually behaves inside | Everything not made by people | *What kind of thing it is
test: Ella goes on a nature trail with her class. What is a nature trail? | *A path through the countryside to look at plants and animals | A type of school bag | A road for cars in a town | A shop that sells pets
exam: «Nature is lovely to look at but not always to touch: cacti in the desert need care.» Which meaning of nature fits this sentence best? | A person's character inside | Only the sky and the weather | *Everything not made by people, the living world | The nature of a school
